WEBVTT

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:14.630
AR15 was arrested on suspicion
of leaking classified information.

00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:18.890
The other members of AR Team
refused to accept this,

00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:18.930
as they went to participate in the
mission to defeat Destroyer.

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:22.100
"Destroyer A Sangvis High-End Model."

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:22.100
as they went to participate in the
mission to defeat Destroyer.

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:31.110
We discovered you were generating
serious errors during data upload.

00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:32.650
That's impossible!

00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:33.610
It must be a mistake!

00:00:33.610 --> 00:00:35.910
Shut up, SOPII.

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:37.490
This isn't your problem.

00:00:37.490 --> 00:00:42.200
If I'm a doll, that means I shouldn't
feel affected. So why do I?

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:46.080
We're just tools to send on missions.

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:50.420
Emergency transmission to all
Griffin dolls and commanders.

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:55.930
AR Team's T-Doll, AR15, escaped the
interrogation room five minutes ago.

00:00:55.930 --> 00:01:00.760
Report to command if you find her,
and apprehend her immediately.

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:04.730
If needed, you are permitted
to attack or destroy her.

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:14.650
Do you really think you
can get away with this?

00:01:14.650 --> 00:01:18.320
You can revive as soon
as you're killed anyway.

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:21.990
You'll lose your memories of
what's happening now, too.

00:01:23.330 --> 00:01:25.410
And when that happens,

00:01:25.410 --> 00:01:29.130
you'll be like a little puppy that
does whatever I tell her to!

00:01:29.130 --> 00:01:31.130
That's... not true!

00:01:31.130 --> 00:01:33.380
You're lying!

00:01:33.380 --> 00:01:34.880
You think so?

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:37.550
My adorable little moron...

00:01:37.550 --> 00:01:41.430
You don't think this is
the first time, do you?

00:01:47.020 --> 00:01:50.980
Y-You jerk! Dummy! Crazy woman!

00:01:50.980 --> 00:01:55.150
Y-You promised to help me!

00:01:58.490 --> 00:02:00.740
Right, right. Don't cry.

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:02.620
I was just joking.

00:02:02.620 --> 00:02:04.450
J-Joking?

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:10.170
Agent's equipped with you
with the data reception key.

00:02:10.170 --> 00:02:12.790
A-Agent did that?

00:02:12.790 --> 00:02:15.800
Yeah, so I'll help you.

00:02:18.050 --> 00:02:22.010
But if you want to get away, you need
to do exactly what I tell you to.

00:02:22.010 --> 00:02:23.510
O-Okay...

00:03:59.030 --> 00:04:01.860
SOPII, what's Destroyer's location?

00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:04.950
She's still in tracking range.
We'll catch up soon.

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:11.250
She stopped moving.

00:04:15.130 --> 00:04:18.250
A flare? Some kind of... beacon?

00:04:18.250 --> 00:04:19.960
She's under it!

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:23.300
Her signal's coming from right there!

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:25.970
It'll take about three minutes
to get there. She's close.

00:04:25.970 --> 00:04:27.930
This doesn't make sense.

00:04:27.930 --> 00:04:31.600
Why reveal your location?

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:35.060
It's obviously a trap.
We can't go any further.

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:39.940
But Destroyer's right there!
We have to keep going!

00:04:39.940 --> 00:04:41.940
It's our mission!

00:04:41.940 --> 00:04:44.530
Isn't that what you said?

00:04:47.490 --> 00:04:48.950
She self-destructed?

00:04:48.950 --> 00:04:52.040
That was the sound of a shell exploding.

00:04:52.040 --> 00:04:55.790
But the impact noise
was a little different.

00:04:55.790 --> 00:04:58.790
It probably wasn't Destroyer.

00:04:58.790 --> 00:05:01.340
She's just getting desperate, that's all!

00:05:01.340 --> 00:05:03.010
Let's forget it and keep going!

00:05:03.010 --> 00:05:05.840
M4, AR Team! Do you read?

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:07.550
What's your situation?

00:05:07.550 --> 00:05:11.140
Commander Gentiane, we're fine!

00:05:11.140 --> 00:05:13.890
AR Team is tracking Destroyer.

00:05:13.890 --> 00:05:16.520
It appears she's attempting
to use a different weapon.

00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:18.190
But it's no threat.

00:05:18.190 --> 00:05:19.690
A different weapon?

00:05:19.690 --> 00:05:22.570
I haven't heard any reports about that.

00:05:22.570 --> 00:05:24.320
Why are you so far ahead?

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:36.620
Commander Gentiane,
call back AR Team, now!

00:05:36.620 --> 00:05:40.840
I think AR Team is capable of
taking out a lone Sangvis Ringleader.

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:44.300
This terrain...

00:05:47.130 --> 00:05:48.090
No!

00:05:48.090 --> 00:05:51.760
AR Team, cease pursuit and
escape as fast as you can!

00:05:51.760 --> 00:05:55.600
But Commander, Destroyer is so close!

00:05:55.600 --> 00:05:57.890
That's no new weapon.

00:05:57.890 --> 00:06:02.070
The artillery that attacked
our base is aiming for you!

00:06:07.490 --> 00:06:10.030
Dreamer, what are you doing?

00:06:10.030 --> 00:06:12.080
That landed right next to me!

00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:16.910
Don't worry. That was a test round.
I put less explosives in it.

00:06:16.910 --> 00:06:20.380
Calculations complete.
Adjustments complete.

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:21.840
All green.

00:06:21.840 --> 00:06:27.550
And AR Team is probably... right here.

00:06:28.680 --> 00:06:32.470
Maybe I'll fire everything I've got
right where I think they are!

00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:55.700
Are you insane?

00:06:55.700 --> 00:06:58.960
Agent said not to kill M4!

00:06:58.960 --> 00:07:03.670
If they're giving me a chance to play
with Jupiter, I'm going to enjoy it!

00:07:06.920 --> 00:07:12.050
And AR Team won't be killed
by a few artillery blasts.

00:07:12.050 --> 00:07:12.970
If anything,

00:07:12.970 --> 00:07:16.470
it'll be easier to bring them back if
they're missing some arms and legs, right?

00:07:18.930 --> 00:07:20.940
AR Team, listen.

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:22.900
Destroyer is a decoy.

00:07:22.900 --> 00:07:26.690
You've been lured inside
Sangvis artillery range.

00:07:26.690 --> 00:07:28.320
Get out of there! Now!

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:30.450
R-Roger!

00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:32.780
Detecting a Sangvis active scan!

00:07:32.780 --> 00:07:35.950
If AR Team is detected,
they won't be able to escape!

00:07:35.950 --> 00:07:38.580
Attention all doll commanders!

00:07:38.580 --> 00:07:40.830
I'm changing your mission objectives!

00:07:40.830 --> 00:07:44.710
Get AR Team out of there
no matter what it takes!

00:07:46.590 --> 00:07:48.510
Roger.

00:07:48.510 --> 00:07:49.760
Damn it!

00:07:50.800 --> 00:07:55.970
All dolls in 794 Unit,
move to coordinates M34Y9.

00:07:55.970 --> 00:07:57.970
Remain in position once you arrive.

00:07:57.970 --> 00:07:59.180
Roger.

00:08:03.520 --> 00:08:07.110
Huh? Are our allies heading toward us?

00:08:07.110 --> 00:08:10.360
Don't get distracted. Focus on moving!

00:08:10.360 --> 00:08:11.700
R-Right!

00:08:16.570 --> 00:08:21.660
Harpoon Team, head from the
west to coordinates M32Y8.

00:08:21.660 --> 00:08:22.500
Roger.

00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:25.460
Longsword, head to M36Y7.

00:08:25.460 --> 00:08:29.880
We didn't expect the enemy to
focus their firepower on AR Team.

00:08:29.880 --> 00:08:31.260
What's going on?

00:08:31.260 --> 00:08:35.180
I don't know, but we
can't let them be found.

00:08:35.180 --> 00:08:40.560
Commander Shi Jun, move your
units towards AR Team.

00:08:40.560 --> 00:08:43.390
We're going to try and confuse
the Sangvis scanning, right?

00:08:43.390 --> 00:08:45.350
Then let's make sure
their routes intersect.

00:08:45.350 --> 00:08:48.060
Fishing Net has reached the point.

00:08:51.110 --> 00:08:55.950
All T-Dolls, open fire on the
Sangvis at point M36Y9!

00:08:55.950 --> 00:08:57.160
Roger!

00:09:00.790 --> 00:09:03.000
Griffin? When did they...?

00:09:04.250 --> 00:09:06.960
Dreamer! Griffin's here!

00:09:08.670 --> 00:09:11.500
That's not AR Team.

00:09:11.500 --> 00:09:13.920
Deal with them yourself, why don't you?

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:16.680
If they get any closer,
I'll be in big trouble!

00:09:16.680 --> 00:09:20.680
God, you're a pain.

00:09:20.680 --> 00:09:22.720
I guess I'll take them all out!

00:09:25.440 --> 00:09:28.060
It's your job to make sure
you get to a safe distance.

00:09:28.060 --> 00:09:30.020
O-Okay!

00:09:41.950 --> 00:09:44.700
Commander! The artillery's
targeting a different direction!

00:09:44.700 --> 00:09:46.920
It's hitting another unit!

00:09:46.920 --> 00:09:48.830
Run! Don't stop for anything!

00:09:50.090 --> 00:09:52.500
Run as fast as you can into that valley!

00:09:56.590 --> 00:09:57.800
Okay!

00:10:11.940 --> 00:10:15.190
This is a fun little toy.

00:10:18.110 --> 00:10:21.530
I wonder if I let AR Team get away?

00:10:23.830 --> 00:10:25.580
Well, it doesn't matter.

00:10:25.580 --> 00:10:29.750
Destroyer, you've got ten
minutes to get out of there.

00:10:29.750 --> 00:10:31.710
O-Okay.

00:10:31.710 --> 00:10:33.590
This is the last time.

00:10:33.590 --> 00:10:35.260
The next time you let someone
bug your communications,

00:10:35.260 --> 00:10:37.840
I really will leave you to die.

00:10:37.840 --> 00:10:40.430
I'm bugged? By who? When?

00:10:43.300 --> 00:10:45.470
When did you find me?

00:10:45.470 --> 00:10:49.020
She who rules the sky, rules everything.

00:10:49.020 --> 00:10:55.110
Without any thermal camo, you stuck
out as much as our own little idiot.

00:10:55.110 --> 00:10:58.400
I guess disguising my
signal wasn't enough.

00:10:58.400 --> 00:11:00.860
You've been waiting for this chance
this whole time, haven't you?

00:11:00.860 --> 00:11:06.750
While I was focusing on your friends,
you snuck close to her.

00:11:06.750 --> 00:11:10.500
Guess you're not as
crazy as Destroyer says.

00:11:10.500 --> 00:11:14.880
And you're not as cold as the data says.

00:11:14.880 --> 00:11:18.090
I suppose I should give you credit
for your courage in coming here,

00:11:18.090 --> 00:11:21.050
instead of running away.

00:11:21.050 --> 00:11:22.260
Now that you've found me,

00:11:22.260 --> 00:11:25.600
I suppose the artillery shell will be
arriving in the next ten seconds.

00:11:25.600 --> 00:11:27.220
Of course not!

00:11:27.220 --> 00:11:29.640
You're still worth using.

00:11:29.640 --> 00:11:33.100
AR15, you've been chosen.

00:11:34.810 --> 00:11:39.610
The power we gave you... did you like it?

00:11:39.610 --> 00:11:42.780
How do you have Sangvis command authority?

00:11:44.280 --> 00:11:47.790
So it was your doing!

00:11:47.790 --> 00:11:49.950
Don't get so upset.

00:11:49.950 --> 00:11:53.380
If you knew you were leaking information,

00:11:53.380 --> 00:11:56.380
why didn't you tell your comrades sooner?

00:11:56.380 --> 00:12:01.220
If you had, that dumb girl never would've
been able to find the Griffin base.

00:12:01.220 --> 00:12:04.590
S-So I was just a tool being
used in some other plan?

00:12:04.590 --> 00:12:09.270
AR15, satisfy my curiosity!

00:12:09.270 --> 00:12:14.440
You're a doll, but you disobey
your employer's orders! Why?

00:12:15.730 --> 00:12:20.900
You used me to leak information
that put my comrades in danger.

00:12:23.070 --> 00:12:26.570
You'll pay for this, Sangvis.

00:12:26.570 --> 00:12:29.740
That doesn't answer my question!

00:12:29.740 --> 00:12:32.710
But now you know everything
that's going on. Congratulations!

00:12:33.830 --> 00:12:36.710
Want one last futile attempt
to change things?

00:12:36.710 --> 00:12:40.670
To see if your final pathetic struggle
can make this all better?

00:12:42.970 --> 00:12:44.300
Maybe it will!

00:12:44.300 --> 00:12:47.180
That's the plan, Dreamer.

00:12:47.180 --> 00:12:49.970
Until everything becomes clear...

00:12:49.970 --> 00:12:51.930
...I'm going to keep struggling!

00:12:55.230 --> 00:13:00.530
I'm going to bring my boot down on your
face and reveal every one of your plans!

00:13:00.530 --> 00:13:03.400
Get ready, Sangvis scum!

00:13:04.070 --> 00:13:07.070
"One Week Later Griffin-Held Territory
Forward Operating Base 794"

00:13:13.000 --> 00:13:14.210
What's the situation?

00:13:15.620 --> 00:13:18.750
The Neural Cloud
backups are all installed.

00:13:18.750 --> 00:13:22.050
They're all using the
same bodies they were.

00:13:22.050 --> 00:13:25.510
But they'll need individual adjustments.

00:13:25.510 --> 00:13:26.720
Yeah.

00:13:36.730 --> 00:13:42.320
I think I understand why the boss uses
guns for the names of his T-Dolls.

00:13:44.360 --> 00:13:50.030
If he used human names, you'd feel
guilty every time one was destroyed.

00:13:50.030 --> 00:13:53.160
And what's worse is...

00:13:55.960 --> 00:13:58.290
Helian!

00:13:58.290 --> 00:14:01.630
If AR Team had withdrawn quickly,

00:14:01.630 --> 00:14:05.920
it's highly likely they would've
escaped Sangvis's artillery range.

00:14:05.920 --> 00:14:10.010
Why did Kryuger use the
other units as decoys?

00:14:10.010 --> 00:14:13.430
What did we sacrifice them for?

00:14:19.350 --> 00:14:23.650
Commander Gentiane,
I've read your mission logs.

00:14:23.650 --> 00:14:27.280
You seem to care deeply for the T-Dolls.

00:14:27.280 --> 00:14:31.030
If you're not satisfied with how the
mission turned out, I can understand that.

00:14:31.030 --> 00:14:33.870
But there's one thing I
want you to remember:

00:14:33.870 --> 00:14:39.960
AR Team are an experiment created
by 16LAB, IOP's research unit.

00:14:39.960 --> 00:14:42.170
The structure of their minds
are completely different

00:14:42.170 --> 00:14:43.550
than that of other T- Dolls.

00:14:43.550 --> 00:14:46.510
They have emotions. Thoughts.

00:14:46.510 --> 00:14:52.260
That makes their mental efficiency
several times greater than other models.

00:14:52.260 --> 00:14:55.270
That much, I know you've been told.

00:14:55.270 --> 00:15:01.020
But because of that, they can't make
backups of their Neural Clouds.

00:15:05.320 --> 00:15:09.570
They're the most advanced
T-Dolls Griffin has.

00:15:09.570 --> 00:15:12.410
For a PMC that uses dolls
as its main fighting force,

00:15:12.410 --> 00:15:15.740
they're our most valuable asset.

00:15:15.740 --> 00:15:21.710
That's why they must be kept operational,
even if others must be sacrificed.

00:15:22.790 --> 00:15:25.630
Does that answer your question?

00:15:25.630 --> 00:15:29.720
You're a talented doll commander.

00:15:29.720 --> 00:15:34.050
And I can see you've built a good
relationship with AR Team.

00:15:34.050 --> 00:15:38.680
You may get another
chance to command them.

00:15:38.680 --> 00:15:41.350
When that happens, be careful.

00:15:54.200 --> 00:15:58.240
What is AR Team doing right now, I wonder?

00:16:02.290 --> 00:16:04.630
Where's all this firepower coming from?

00:16:04.630 --> 00:16:08.090
The mission report said
the Sangvis retreated.

00:16:08.090 --> 00:16:13.430
Helian told us all we had to do was patrol
the area where we fought last time!

00:16:13.430 --> 00:16:17.060
And when that was over, we could
go back to Gentiane's base.

00:16:17.060 --> 00:16:20.430
You really do like that commander.

00:16:20.430 --> 00:16:21.640
Damn it!

00:16:24.520 --> 00:16:25.730
Huh?

00:16:27.730 --> 00:16:29.280
Level VI body armor!

00:16:29.280 --> 00:16:31.530
We can't penetrate it at this range!

00:16:31.530 --> 00:16:32.900
A new type of Sangvis?

00:16:32.900 --> 00:16:36.200
I don't know! I've never seen them before!

00:16:36.200 --> 00:16:39.580
They're not moving like Sangvis.
Are they human?

00:16:39.580 --> 00:16:42.040
But this is a yellow area!

00:16:42.040 --> 00:16:44.830
Could humans with that much equipment...

00:16:45.960 --> 00:16:48.960
We've got permission
to fire if we need to,

00:16:48.960 --> 00:16:51.170
but it'll make a mess of
things if we kill a human.

00:16:51.170 --> 00:16:54.220
This is still
Griffin-controlled territory.

00:16:54.220 --> 00:16:57.640
Taking out criminals and
bandits is part of our job.

00:17:00.470 --> 00:17:03.600
I've shared 14 plans with you that
wouldn't result in their deaths.

00:17:03.600 --> 00:17:06.480
Let's go with plan one,
and then stay flexible.

00:17:06.480 --> 00:17:07.690
Go!

00:17:21.870 --> 00:17:23.080
Damn it!

00:17:24.370 --> 00:17:26.250
Hands up!

00:17:26.250 --> 00:17:32.010
You are illegally trespassing on territory
held by a private military contractor!

00:17:32.010 --> 00:17:34.720
This is your last warning! Hands up!

00:17:34.720 --> 00:17:36.470
We have permission to fire!

00:17:41.140 --> 00:17:43.560
They weren't using their full strength.

00:17:43.560 --> 00:17:45.690
But you did well.

00:17:45.690 --> 00:17:48.900
You chose an innovative
way to get us to disarm.

00:17:48.900 --> 00:17:52.070
The warning was a little wimpy, though.

00:17:52.070 --> 00:17:54.400
Don't move. I really will shoot.

00:17:54.400 --> 00:17:57.990
You don't have the right to fire at me.

00:18:00.910 --> 00:18:03.410
I'm sorry, Kryuger!

00:18:03.410 --> 00:18:05.250
What are you doing here?

00:18:05.250 --> 00:18:10.540
Not using your IFF when in our
territory is extremely dangerous.

00:18:12.090 --> 00:18:14.420
They're all human contractors?

00:18:14.420 --> 00:18:16.800
We have our own mission.

00:18:16.800 --> 00:18:19.680
Your mission is over.

00:18:19.680 --> 00:18:21.850
Guard the transport team.

00:18:23.140 --> 00:18:26.730
We're a special operations team,
not security guards!

00:18:26.730 --> 00:18:28.560
SOPII, calm down.

00:18:32.690 --> 00:18:34.730
What the hell is going on?

00:18:34.730 --> 00:18:38.530
You refused our request to look for AR15.

00:18:38.530 --> 00:18:41.700
And now you've got us running errands?

00:18:41.700 --> 00:18:46.790
SOPII, you asked me before
why we had emotion models

00:18:46.790 --> 00:18:50.130
when we're just tools, right?

00:18:50.130 --> 00:18:53.090
Emotions are a defect.

00:18:53.090 --> 00:18:56.800
Humans just created the same
defect within us that they have.

00:18:56.800 --> 00:19:01.010
So don't expect sympathy
from them, especially now.

00:19:01.010 --> 00:19:04.510
M16, I didn't understand that at all!

00:19:04.510 --> 00:19:07.430
I didn't really understand it myself,
and I'm the one who said it!

00:19:07.430 --> 00:19:10.150
It's just a little argument
for us AIs to enjoy.

00:19:12.060 --> 00:19:16.070
But if Kryuger is here,

00:19:16.070 --> 00:19:19.820
that means Griffin hasn't
given up on AR15.

00:19:19.820 --> 00:19:21.700
And we're the same.

00:19:24.580 --> 00:19:29.080
If we believe in each other,
we'll meet again someday.

00:19:47.020 --> 00:19:50.600
"18 Hours Before Mission Start"

00:19:50.980 --> 00:19:53.900
That concludes AR Team's report.

00:19:55.270 --> 00:19:59.030
About the parts you recovered, Kryuger.

00:19:59.030 --> 00:20:04.120
Some of them matched parts
made in Sangvis Ferri facilities.

00:20:04.120 --> 00:20:10.710
For the Armored T-Doll Aegis and
Tactical Mechanized Infantry Nemeum.

00:20:10.710 --> 00:20:14.380
The remainder don't
match any known models.

00:20:15.790 --> 00:20:17.880
Unknown weapons...

00:20:19.960 --> 00:20:22.840
That artillery that attacked our base?

00:20:22.840 --> 00:20:24.760
Likely so.

00:20:24.760 --> 00:20:27.720
Kryuger, this means...

00:20:27.720 --> 00:20:30.640
The Sangvis are evolving.

00:20:30.640 --> 00:20:33.650
They've gone beyond
our expectations already.

00:20:33.650 --> 00:20:40.570
The one thing we do know is
that Parapluie is a T-Doll virus.

00:20:40.570 --> 00:20:43.530
And the most effective way
for Sangvis to break the cordon

00:20:43.530 --> 00:20:45.620
is to attempt to infect our dolls.

00:20:45.620 --> 00:20:50.000
It looks like they intend to do
everything they can to wipe out Griffin.

00:20:52.160 --> 00:20:58.210
And Aegis and Nemeum were both
manufactured in the Sangvis factory

00:20:58.210 --> 00:21:01.170
that was our target in that mission.

00:21:03.800 --> 00:21:09.140
Tactical Doll AR15 is the key
that connects all these hints.

00:21:09.140 --> 00:21:12.730
We need to get the information
about Parapluie out of her mind,

00:21:12.730 --> 00:21:15.350
no matter what state she's in.

00:21:15.350 --> 00:21:17.610
And that means finding
her before the Sangvis!

00:21:17.610 --> 00:21:22.490
But we won't be able to ensure
her safety then, Kryuger.

00:21:24.070 --> 00:21:27.370
I don't hold any prejudices towards dolls.

00:21:29.580 --> 00:21:32.200
I'm grateful to them for
bearing the responsibility

00:21:32.200 --> 00:21:33.750
of this in humanity's place.

00:21:35.710 --> 00:21:40.840
I can understand why some
commanders treat them like humans.

00:21:42.760 --> 00:21:45.630
But whether they're tools, or friends,

00:21:45.630 --> 00:21:51.220
once they've fallen into enemy hands,
we have to make a decision.

00:21:51.220 --> 00:21:57.100
Take them out ourselves, or watch
helplessly as they drag us all to hell.

00:21:57.100 --> 00:21:58.770
Understood.

00:21:58.770 --> 00:22:02.230
I'll arrange for a check of inventory
and purchase orders.

00:22:02.230 --> 00:22:03.440
Thanks.

00:22:05.360 --> 00:22:06.780
Excuse me.

00:22:19.290 --> 00:22:22.590
This is my highest-priority order,

00:22:22.590 --> 00:22:27.510
both as a T-Doll and a
member of AR Team.

00:22:28.590 --> 00:22:31.550
Even if I've lost my home...

00:22:31.550 --> 00:22:36.850
...I won't betray the first
people to accept me.

00:22:36.850 --> 00:22:42.520
That is the one reason I exist,
the one fate I have.

00:24:43.060 --> 00:24:46.650
Episode 11: "Comet 01."
